<!--
NODrugLiver.DES - Defines liver metabolism of NO in HumMod

Overview
This file models the metabolism of Nitric Oxide (NO) in the liver, specifically how NO is processed from the portal vein into systemic circulation.

1. Portal Vein Drug Concentration: Calculates NO levels in the portal vein, which is where blood from the digestive system enters the liver.
2. Conversion to Different Units: Converts NO mass to different concentration units for calculations.
3. Liver Metabolism Rate: Uses a constant rate (K = 0.75) to define how much NO is processed by the liver.

How to Replicate for Another Drug
1. Change `<name> NODrugLiver </name>` to `<name> NewDrugLiver </name>`.
2. Adjust K (metabolism rate) to match the new drug’s liver metabolism properties.
3. Modify PortalMass calculations to ensure correct mass transport.
4. Reference this file in the main drug model (`NODrug.DES` or equivalent).

-->

HumMod / FurosemideKidney

Created : 05-Jun-06
Last Modified : 26-Jan-10
Author : Tom Coleman
Copyright : 2006-2010
By : University Of Mississippi Medical Center
Schema : DES V1.0

<structure><name> NODrugLiver </name> <!-- Defines NO metabolism in the liver -->

<variables>

<var>
  <name> Gain </name> <!-- Stores the amount of NO entering the liver -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> PortalMass </name> <!-- Mass of NO in the portal vein -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> [PortalMass] </name> <!-- Portal mass in concentration units -->
</var>

<var>
  <name> [PortalMass(uMol)] </name> <!-- Portal mass converted to micromolar units -->
</var>

<constant>
  <name> K </name> <!-- Rate of NO metabolism in the liver, will vary for other drugs -->
  <val> 0.75 </val>
</constant>

</variables>

<definitions>

<block><name> Dervs </name> <!-- Defines how NO is metabolized in the liver -->

<def>
  <name> PortalMass </name>
  <val> SplanchnicVeins.Vol * ( NODrugPool.[NODrug] ) </val> <!-- Computes portal vein NO mass. the value referenced here is what is calculated in the pool -->
</def>

<def>
   <name> [PortalMass] </name>
   <val> PortalMass / SplanchnicVeins.Vol </val> <!-- converts the mass to concentration -->
</def>

<def>
   <name> [PortalMass(uMol)] </name>
   <val> [PortalMass] / NODrugPool.MW </val> <!-- converts concentration to micromolar -->
</def>

<def>
  <name> Gain </name> <!-- rate of NO uptake by the liver -->
  <val> K * PortalMass </val>
</def>

</block>

</definitions>
</structure>

End
